{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-20250514","id":"msg_vrtx_011CdMRwJBuvXzynCVWDy3Rw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to use the sqli-detector skill to analyze a piece of Java code for SQL injection vulnerabilities. Let me look at the code carefully:\n\n1. The code takes a parameter from the HTTP request: `String param = request.getParameter(\"username\");`\n2. It constructs a SQL query: `String sql = \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = ? AND active = 1\";`\n3. It uses a PreparedStatement: `PreparedStatement pstmt = conn.prepareStatement(sql);`\n4. It sets the parameter using the safe method: `pstmt.setString(1, param);`\n5. It executes the query: `ResultSet rs = pstmt.executeQuery();`\n\nThis is a classic example of SAFE code because:\n- The SQL query uses a parameterized placeholder `?` \n- The user input (`param`) is bound to the placeholder using `pstmt.setString(1, param)`\n- There is no direct string concatenation of user input into the SQL query\n\nThis is NOT vulnerable to SQL injection because the PreparedStatement properly parameterizes the query and separates the SQL structure from the data.\n\nI should use the Skill tool to invoke the sqli-detector skill with the provided arguments.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10061,"cache_read_input_tokens":23042,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":10061,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"27f78020-2e16-4bc3-911f-7ae10cc841db","uuid":"cb42e76e-d29a-455d-99a4-e940902e835d","timestamp":"2026-07-24T19:25:30.183Z","request_id":"req_vrtx_011CdMRwJ7CwKrDUeqk9LE5k"}
